data.asynchronous-data-movement--pipeline-sta:
Modern CUDA bypasses intermediate register staging for global-to-shared copies using asynchronous copy instructions:
Code snippet
#include #include // Asynchronous copy directly from Global to Shared Memory (Ampere+ cp.async) __global__ void tiled_async_copy(float* d_in, float* d_out, int N) { extern __shared__ float s_tile[]; int tid = threadIdx.x; int idx = blockIdx.x * blockDim.x + threadIdx.x; // Direct Global -> Shared transfer without touching thread registers cuda::memcpy_async(&s_tile[tid], &d_in[idx], sizeof(float), cuda::aligned_size_t{}); // Asynchronous barrier sync cuda::pipeline_shared_state<cuda::thread_scope_block, 2> shared_state; // Overlap compute on previous tile while waiting for current tile transfer... }

data.cooperative-groups-and-clusters#Cooperat:
CUDA Cooperative Groups replace brittle raw barriers with composable, flexible thread synchronization:
Code snippet
#include namespace cg = cooperative_groups; __global__ void cooperative_kernel() { cg::thread_block block = cg::this_thread_block(); cg::thread_block_tile<32> warp = cg::tiled_partition<32>(block); // Synchronize only the warp, not the whole block warp.sync(); // Cluster-level access (Hopper Architecture: Distributed Shared Memory / DSMEM) // Allows thread blocks within a cluster to read/write each other's shared memory }

data.warp-level-primitives-intra-warp-communi:
Rather than writing to shared memory and calling __syncthreads(), threads within a warp can exchange registers directly in silicon using warp shuffle instructions:
Code snippet
// Intra-warp inclusive sum reduction using shuffle down inline __device__ float warp_reduce_sum(float val) { #pragma unroll for (int offset = 16; offset > 0; offset /= 2) { val += __shfl_down_sync(0xffffffff, val, offset); } return val; // Lane 0 contains the reduction sum of the warp } Active Mask (0xffffffff): Specifies which lanes participate; inactive lanes are ignored. Other primitives include __ballot_sync, __any_sync, and __all_sync for evaluating branch predicates across a warp.

